WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.944
A site shows pictures in several sizes:

00:00:03.944 --> 00:00:06.692
a banner, a thumbnail, a card image.

00:00:06.692 --> 00:00:12.123
Media profiles give each size a name, so every page produces it the same way.

00:00:12.123 --> 00:00:17.750
You will create a profile, learn the resize modes, and see a change on the site.

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:26.208
A picture uploaded to the Media Library keeps its own size, but a

00:00:26.208 --> 00:00:30.282
page needs it wide for a banner, small for a thumbnail, and different

00:00:30.282 --> 00:00:31.532
again for a card.

00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:35.770
Spelling those sizes out in every page makes them hard to keep the same.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.832
A media profile is a named set of image settings, such as width,

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:43.666
height, resize mode, format and quality.

00:00:43.666 --> 00:00:47.794
A theme asks for it by name, and Orchard Core makes the image

00:00:47.794 --> 00:00:49.457
when a page needs it.

00:00:49.457 --> 00:00:51.860
The original file stays as it is.

00:00:56.076 --> 00:00:59.214
In the admin menu, open Media, then Profiles.

00:00:59.214 --> 00:01:04.322
The Media Profiles page lists each profile by name, with its hint underneath.

00:01:04.322 --> 00:01:10.476
By default, only administrators have the Manage Media Profiles permission that the page needs.

00:01:10.944 --> 00:01:15.048
This site comes from the Blog recipe, which adds one profile:

00:01:15.048 --> 00:01:15.844
banner.

00:01:15.844 --> 00:01:20.192
Its hint describes a banner image of 2048 by 600 pixels, cropped.

00:01:20.192 --> 00:01:24.112
The Blog theme uses it for the large picture at the top of

00:01:24.112 --> 00:01:26.684
the home page, posts and About page.

00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:29.855
The search box filters the list by name.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:34.278
Each row has Edit and Delete buttons, and Add Media Profile opens the

00:01:34.278 --> 00:01:36.283
form that creates a profile.

00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:45.183
The Resize Mode setting decides how a picture meets the width and height.

00:01:45.183 --> 00:01:50.301
Max, the default, fits the whole picture inside them, keeps its proportions, and

00:01:50.301 --> 00:01:52.502
never enlarges a small picture.

00:01:52.502 --> 00:01:57.263
Crop makes a large picture fill the size, cutting away what falls outside.

00:01:58.013 --> 00:02:03.079
Pad also fits the whole picture, then fills the empty space with a Background Color.

00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:07.639
Stretch forces the picture to the exact width and height, which distorts it

00:02:07.639 --> 00:02:09.553
when the proportions differ.

00:02:13.761 --> 00:02:16.487
Let's create a profile for thumbnails.

00:02:16.487 --> 00:02:21.941
On the Media Profiles page, Add Media Profile opens the Create Media Profile form.

00:02:22.399 --> 00:02:23.923
The Name is required.

00:02:23.923 --> 00:02:27.932
A theme asks for the profile by this name, and Orchard Core saves

00:02:27.932 --> 00:02:30.586
it in lowercase, so let's type thumbnail.

00:02:30.586 --> 00:02:34.709
The Hint is a note for your team, shown under the name in the list.

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:39.884
Width and Height each offer a list of sizes in pixels, and Default

00:02:39.884 --> 00:02:42.176
applies no size to that side.

00:02:42.176 --> 00:02:46.696
Custom Size shows a box for any other number, so let's type 320

00:02:46.696 --> 00:02:49.447
for Width and choose 240 for Height.

00:02:49.907 --> 00:02:55.427
Let's set Resize Mode to Crop, so a large picture fills the whole thumbnail size.

00:02:55.427 --> 00:03:01.137
The Background Color field stays hidden, because it appears only for Pad and BoxPad.

00:03:01.607 --> 00:03:06.918
Format converts the image, and Default keeps the format of the original.

00:03:06.918 --> 00:03:13.319
Quality is a percentage for Jpg and WebP images, and at 100 the default quality applies.

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:16.247
Let's choose Jpg and a quality of 80.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.007
Auto Orient is ticked by default.

00:03:19.007 --> 00:03:23.739
It turns the image to match the orientation recorded in its EXIF metadata.

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:27.880
Save adds the profile to the list, with the hint under the name.

00:03:32.086 --> 00:03:33.528
This is the home page.

00:03:33.528 --> 00:03:37.393
The large picture behind the title is a photo from the Media Library,

00:03:37.393 --> 00:03:39.866
cut to a wide strip by the banner profile.

00:03:40.347 --> 00:03:44.197
The Blog theme asks for banner on the home page, on blog posts,

00:03:44.197 --> 00:03:45.759
and on the About page.

00:03:45.759 --> 00:03:48.437
A change to the profile changes all three.

00:03:48.899 --> 00:03:52.914
Back on the Media Profiles page, let's choose Edit for banner.

00:03:52.914 --> 00:03:56.989
The form has the same fields as the one that creates a profile.

00:03:57.445 --> 00:04:00.245
Let's choose Pad as the Resize Mode.

00:04:00.245 --> 00:04:05.311
The Background Color field appears, so let's type a color code for the

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.245
empty space, such as 336699, and save.

00:04:08.706 --> 00:04:11.971
On the home page, the photo sits in the middle of the header,

00:04:11.971 --> 00:04:13.676
with the color on both sides.

00:04:14.127 --> 00:04:18.877
A blog post shows the same change, because its header uses the same profile.

00:04:23.078 --> 00:04:26.963
On the Media Profiles page, to find a profile, type part of its

00:04:26.963 --> 00:04:29.496
name in the search box and press Enter.

00:04:29.496 --> 00:04:32.198
The list shows only the matching profiles.

00:04:32.656 --> 00:04:34.698
Edit also lets you rename a profile.

00:04:34.698 --> 00:04:37.955
A theme that asks for the old name gets none of the profile's

00:04:37.955 --> 00:04:40.386
settings, so change the theme with the name.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.714
Delete asks you to confirm, and then removes the profile.

00:04:44.714 --> 00:04:48.280
Let's delete thumbnail, so that only banner remains.

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.584
That is how media profiles work:

00:04:52.584 --> 00:04:57.132
one name for each image size, created in Media, Profiles, and used by

00:04:57.132 --> 00:04:59.194
every page that asks for it.

00:04:59.194 --> 00:05:00.770
Thanks for watching.

